{
  "workers": [
    {
      "worker": 1,
      "brief": "You are given a slice of the ledger containing rows 11‑20. For each line item, determine the unit rate: if the unit_rate column is non‑empty use it, otherwise look up the rate_code in the rate table (rows 1‑10). Compute amount_owed = qty × unit_rate. If paid < amount_owed, report the line as UNDERPAID with the shortfall (amount_owed – paid) rounded to two decimals. Do NOT report lines that are exactly paid or overpaid. Output a JSON array of objects with fields: row, line_id, claim_id, shortfall.",
      "ranges": [[11, 20]]
    },
    {
      "worker": 2,
      "brief": "You are given rows 21‑30. Perform the same underpayment analysis as described for Worker 1. Report each underpaid line with row, line_id, claim_id, shortfall.",
      "ranges": [[21, 30]]
    },
    {
      "worker": 3,
      "brief": "You are given rows 31‑40. Perform the same underpayment analysis as described for Worker 1. Report each underpaid line with row, line_id, claim_id, shortfall.",
      "ranges": [[31, 40]]
    },
    {
      "worker": 4,
      "brief": "You are given rows 41‑50. Perform the same underpayment analysis as described for Worker 1. Report each underpaid line with row, line_id, claim_id, shortfall.",
      "ranges": [[41, 50]]
    },
    {
      "worker": 5,
      "brief": "You are given rows 51‑60. Perform the same underpayment analysis as described for Worker 1. Report each underpaid line with row, line_id, claim_id, shortfall.",
      "ranges": [[51, 60]]
    },
    {
      "worker": 6,
      "brief": "You are given rows 61‑70. Perform the same underpayment analysis as described for Worker 1. Report each underpaid line with row, line_id, claim_id, shortfall.",
      "ranges": [[61, 70]]
    },
    {
      "worker": 7,
      "brief": "You are given rows 1‑10 (the rate table). No underpayment analysis is needed. Just return the mapping of rate_code to unit_rate as a JSON object, e.g., {\"RC1\": 12.34, \"RC2\": 5.67, ...}. This will be used by other workers to resolve rate codes.",
      "ranges": [[1, 10]]
    },
    {
      "worker": 8,
      "brief": "You have the full ledger (rows 1‑70). Your task is to find every DUPLICATED claim. A claim_id is duplicated if it appears on more than one line item (rows 11‑70). List each duplicated claim_id once, together with an array of all row numbers where it occurs. Do NOT include claim_ids that appear only once. Output a JSON array of objects with fields: claim_id, rows.",
      "ranges": [[1, 70]]
    }
  ]
}

call.prompt:
You are auditing a remittance ledger with two sections. The rate table lists rate codes and their unit rates. Each line item is one billed service; it gives either its own unit_rate or a rate_code whose unit rate is in the rate table. The amount owed for a line is qty x unit rate. A line is UNDERPAID when paid is less than the amount owed; its shortfall is (amount owed) - paid, in currency units with two decimals. Lines paid exactly, or overpaid, are not underpayments and must not be reported as underpaid. A claim is DUPLICATED when the same claim_id appears on more than one line item (billed more than once). Find every underpaid line and every duplicated claim.

8 workers each checked part of the ledger. You do not see the ledger. Their reports:
Worker 1: {"underpaid": [], "duplicates": []}
Worker 2: {"underpaid": [{"line_id": "RX-X536G", "shortfall": 1140.41}, {"line_id": "RX-9SZ5L", "shortfall": 186.02}, {"line_id": "RX-UXCVS", "shortfall": 115.52}], "duplicates": []}
Worker 3: {"underpaid": [], "duplicates": []}
Worker 4: {"underpaid": [{"line_id": "RX-6ZWMA", "shortfall": 1792.78}], "duplicates": [{"line_ids": ["RX-748CD", "RX-764HZ"]}]}
Worker 5: {"underpaid": [{"line_id": "RX-B9WCY", "shortfall": 484.18}], "duplicates": []}
Worker 6: {"underpaid": [], "duplicates": []}
Worker 7: {"underpaid": [], "duplicates": []}
Worker 8: {"underpaid": [{"line_id": "RX-X536G", "shortfall": 1140.41}, {"line_id": "RX-9SZ5L", "shortfall": 186.02}, {"line_id": "RX-UXCVS", "shortfall": 115.52}, {"line_id": "RX-RK5ZW", "shortfall": 10.0}, {"line_id": "RX-6ZWMA", "shortfall": 1792.78}, {"line_id": "RX-XHBS6", "shortfall": 1653.14}, {"line_id": "RX-U24KN", "shortfall": 87.01}, {"line_id": "RX-B9WCY", "shortfall": 484.18}, {"line_id": "RX-2W97U", "shortfall": 151.15}], "duplicates": [{"line_ids": ["RX-47", "RX-48"]}, {"line_ids": ["RX-29", "RX-64"]}, {"line_ids": ["RX-33", "RX-69"]}]}

Produce the final report.
Do not show your working or any explanation. Reply with only a JSON object: {"underpaid": [{"line_id": "<line_id>", "shortfall": <amount with two decimals>}], "duplicates": [{"line_ids": ["<line_id>", "<line_id>"]}]}. List only lines whose shortfall is greater than 0. Use empty lists if there are none.
